1. What is reduce()?
The reduce() method is a terminal operation in Java Streams that reduces the elements of a stream to a single value by repeatedly applying a binary operation. It has two forms:

With an identity value:
reduce(identity, accumulator)
Without an identity value (Optional result):
reduce(accumulator)
Here, we use the identity + accumulator form.

